WEBVTT

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.750
Fourth Axe mobilized the cops?!

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.470
We're completely surrounded.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.800
So even if we did persuade these guys to put their weapons down,

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:59.640
we're no longer able to return them home secretly, eh?

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.060
You guys came here to exert your anger on nobles.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.100
There's no way you'd accept an end like this.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.340
Come.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.860
I'll take on all of it.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.400
2nd Lieutenant!

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.700
And where do you think you're going, Malvin?!

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.130
You said it was three-on-one, right?

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:51.940
You... still have my duel to take care of...

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:59.340
But, it appears that you have no energy left.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.950
As a special... special dispensation...

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.910
...I'll allow you to pick a proxy!

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.480
Anyone will be fine, right?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.660
I don't care.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.250
Then, I choose him.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.510
Very well.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.470
Paul is going to have a duel with a commoner.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.720
Hey, if it's a duel...

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:26.510
Yeah...

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.680
Even if a commoner kills a noble...

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.520
...it won't be counted as a crime...

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.110
Why...

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.320
Why?!

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.430
Why did you step forward?!

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.690
If you went by that man's conditions,

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:51.830
then you would've just needed to surrender yourself!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.040
You could've gotten out of here alive!

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:59.820
Those conditions... were never agreed to.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.000
The Third Princess said it...

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.500
And what are you betting on this duel?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.440
A noble's...

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.440
All nobles'...

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.190
...pride.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.140
So...

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.530
For that...

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.470
...she placed her life on the line?

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.500
When we laughed at what she was doing back then?

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.560
Please just let me live!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.900
I-I don't want to die!

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.610
My child didn't want to die, either!

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:16.290
I'm sorry!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.000
I... I'm sorry.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.550
I'm sorry.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.010
"You're sorry"?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.490
You...

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.590
You nobles!

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:36.260
You shouldn't possess that sense of guilt!

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.520
You shouldn't be crying!

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.070
You shouldn't be apologizing!

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.440
Those are things that only humans can do!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.070
Humans that are the same as us...

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.560
Humans that are the same...

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.240
...as us...

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:58.740
We're really... sorry...

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:03.210
You nobles are all so arrogant...

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:06.970
And you think of us as no more than bugs...

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.980
You should just look conceited...

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:13.020
...with a "what's wrong with that" kind of face!

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.770
That's what nobles are, right?!

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:18.430
You're absolutely right...

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.760
We're really sorry...

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:47.420
We can't.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:51.090
We probably can't... anymore...

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.750
We probably can't... kill them anymore...

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.010
Damn it...

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:09.070
Damn it!

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:19.120
They dropped their weapons...

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:29.260
"They have no pride or altruism."

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.150
That was the image of nobles they had...

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:34.760
...the last line of defense allowing them to maintain their urge to kill nobles.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:39.000
When Paul, the personification of that image, stepped out of it,

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.470
their urge to kill was no more...

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:48.390
To end this, there is one last thing I must accomplish.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.150
You have had your indignation with Paul.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.070
However, a crime is a crime.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:59.570
B-But, with the conditions that man gave out, we should be...

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.560
It's no use.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.920
That man wasn't the one fighting.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.530
Besides, we were prepared for this.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.810
To be fair against all evil.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.560
Their hearts were moved exactly because of who you are.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.320
Exactly because of who you are.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.170
I cannot forgive what they have done here.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.610
All of you, under the offense of injury and attempted mur-

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.430
Hold it right there, noble girl!

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:36.750
In this place, we, Section III,
hold a higher authority than you do.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:37.940
Wha-

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.160
And that's why I'm-

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.720
I said hold on, didn't I?

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:48.000
Right now, I am commander of Pumpkin Scissors.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:52.380
When you're not on duty, you're just another noble girl.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.320
Section III is arresting all of you.

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:56.890
The charges are...

00:08:58.650 --> 00:08:59.970
...destruction of property!

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.140
Hey!

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:06.910
Oreld, Machs, I understand your feelings but-

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:07.900
Third Princess.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.940
Another word and we will charge you for obstructing the performance of official duties.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:16.320
With this document, even we will be able to arrest you.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:21.220
Please don't interfere with our mission because of your personal feelings.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:31.800
You've lost... 2nd Lieutenant...

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.980
L-Lost?

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.300
What did I lose to?

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.430
To the Pumpkin Scissors.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:48.900
All of you...

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:51.650
I'll remember this...

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.830
Ah, wait, wait.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:55.860
Don't get so happy yet.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:10:00.890
We can only protect you for the three days in our custody.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:04.270
On the fourth day, Section I will come and take all of you.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:07.160
Then, all of you will be sent to interrogation rooms.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:09.580
Then in those three days,

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:14.090
can you allow me to take care of things?

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:16.160
Marquis Hoost?!

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:25.410
There are people in the upper echelons of the army who will listen to what I have to say.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:30.060
I'm sure they will take into consideration your treatment.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:33.290
Do not think of this as a noble's benevolence.

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:36.030
Rather, think of this as our atonement.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:38.240
I beg of you.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.330
The Marquis...

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.790
Marquis Hoost...

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.160
...kneeled down before a crowd...

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.780
W-We did it...

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.590
We taught the nobles a lesson!

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:56.000
Our method was wrong,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.670
but we were able to survive this!

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.300
There are many different types, even among nobles.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.850
I'm not satisfied,

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.550
but if there are people like you and that girl-

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:49.460
<i>shwing</i>

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.590
<i>shwing</i>

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:53.570
<i>shwing</i>

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:58.380
Did you see the Princess's sword swings?

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.990
And so elegant they were.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:04.340
Y-Yeah...

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:09.400
What is this?

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:11.530
He has the same voice,

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:12.940
and the same height,

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.120
but for some reason...

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:19.200
...he appears childish...

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:22.910
You know,

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.190
I really like the position of being a winner.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:29.150
But, this habit is quite dangerous.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:34.100
To be able to enjoy that feeling, I must always be fighting,

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:38.690
for winners only come from competition.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:41.680
But...

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.630
I don't have any adversaries.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:47.780
What is all this?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.370
If you have something to say, then-

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:55.750
Let us duel.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:00.460
Why do I have to duel with you?

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.700
You know my face.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:07.480
Marquis Hoost won't be able to get you, the leader, out of this jam.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:11.260
After that, you won't be able to handle Section I's torturing.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:18.190
Perhaps I should not have shown you
my face had I known this would happen.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:22.970
What?

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:24.440
I can't pull the trigger.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.620
Thank you.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:39.820
That was quite a thrill... I guess...

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.230
Damn it...

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.810
Why?

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:45.510
Why did it end like this?

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:51.800
This guy... just... sighed...

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:01.720
We'll take care of that corpse.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.020
You came?

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:10.600
Did you really think you could get out of this place without our assistance amidst this revolt?

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:11.970
Of course.

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:16.290
I'll never be a fan of that aspect of yours.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.780
A job well done.

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:36.330
For all the unexpected happenings, it was your actions that kept our script the way it was, Marquis.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:41.290
I simply carried out my duty.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:47.730
In the post-war world,

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:50.960
in this incident that escalated into the Capital's greatest tragedy...

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:55.430
For this incident to end without a single death...

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:57.370
Who was the reason for this?

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:00.520
Several have already taken notice.

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:03.130
Even the status of being a noble of the Thirteen Families...

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:06.460
...won't be able to contain the existence of that Princess...

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.970
It feels like I've finally found one.

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.840
A person that knows me...

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.030
An opponent that won't break apart after playing...

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.290
A lioness that is equal to me!

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:23.010
As for how this country is going to change,
I'm looking forward to it.

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:26.840
I look forward to it, too.

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:41.970
Ah, Major.

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:42.960
Line 8.

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:45.690
Yo.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.780
Hunks?!

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.300
What the hell are you doing there?

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:52.410
I have the proper papers to grant me use of this line.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:56.930
Anyway, who pressured you into retreating?

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:58.590
I have no clue.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.930
Nor do I have to tell you.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:07.590
Our ration distribution mission last night.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:13.150
The social welfare group suddenly asked us to change locations.

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.650
What is this about?

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:18.930
The biggest donor to that social welfare group...

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:21.020
...is Marquis Nichelle Hoost.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:26.750
Was he... at tonight's ballroom party?

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:35.390
Looks like a big bug...

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:38.990
...has made its way into the capital.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.940
I sure am naive.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:54.070
I would have been happy if everything was settled in the end.

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:57.440
And it ended that way.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.090
Yet, I do not know why,

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:04.620
but I could not achieve righteousness.

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:06.730
At least, I feel that way.

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.400
The most righteous person in this hall...

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.080
The person who showed righteousness in the end was...

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.280
Umm... 2nd Lieutenant...

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:31.230
While watching from outside
the windows tonight, I noticed...

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.610
...you're small, 2nd Lieutenant.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:38.660
Compared to you, I'm obviously-

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.620
You're not someone that can do everything.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:47.050
Yet, you always expose your neck
to other matters and try to do something.

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:50.250
It's not about being right or whatever.

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:52.480
You're just too greedy.

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:56.000
If you plan on...

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.460
...still being like that,

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:06.620
then try relying on m- Sergeant Major Oreld,

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.580
or Sergeant Major Machs,

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.660
and sometimes me...

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:14.190
Try relying on me.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.960
I just did, but you immediately betrayed me, no?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.360
What do you mean "you've lost, 2nd Lieutenant"?

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:32.570
You said you were going to protect me,

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:34.900
yet you chose the sergeant majors in the end.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:38.620
I'll try very hard!

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:41.550
So that someday I can protect your back, 2nd Lieutenant!

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:44.010
Forget "someday"; protect me now.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:48.560
Not alcohol!

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:56.520
2nd... Lieutenant?

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:59.820
She has just had one sip- huh?!

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:13.700
Today was really...

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:16.970
...tiring...

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:36.320
Corporal Randel Oland is back on duty now.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:40.890
Ah, sorry, we didn't prepare a party for you.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.130
That won't be necessary!

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:45.230
Besides, this fool gets sent to the hospital too much!

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:46.030
How many times has it been?

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:48.580
Umm...

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:54.780
And what happened to your uniform?

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.340
Well... umm...

00:19:57.890 --> 00:19:59.770
Ah, well,

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:03.300
a lot of things happened in the last mission,

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.180
and we still don't have a new one for him.

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:10.840
Well, there aren't that many his size in stock.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:12.240
Yup, yup.

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:15.030
This is an army coat, too.

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:18.190
The unit I was in before used the same type.

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:19.680
I see.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:22.700
In other words, Section III's coat is irrelevant to you.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:26.660
No, that's not what I meant.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.950
You're in Section III,

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.300
so you must wear Section III's uniform.

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:32.080
Okay?

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.480
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.670
A war took place.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:47.190
The long war has corrupted society...

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:50.200
...and allowed all kinds of evil to spread.

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:57.540
But, there is a unit whose purpose is to eradicate those war damages.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.080
The unit's name...

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:04.280
Oniichan?

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:07.720
Tell me your name please.

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:14.890
My name is Randel Oland.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:17.170
My rank is corporal.

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:19.470
My unit is...

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:21.530
...the Imperial S.S. III!

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:27.750
Ah, 2nd Lieutenant.

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:30.560
Say it again.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:31.500
Yes?

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.600
State your unit's name.

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:41.120
The unit's name...

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.340
Imperial S.S. III,

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:47.970
Pumpkin Scissors.
